# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in the values you want to use.

# Clerk publishable key (client-side). When set, the SPA shows sign-in / user
# menu controls in the header and enables the post-generation feedback
# widget. When unset, the site runs in anon-only mode — all features still
# work via the per-IP rate limit, just no sign-in UI and no feedback widget.
# This is the "path C" launch configuration.
#
# To enable Clerk auth, you'll also need to set CLERK_SECRET_KEY on the api
# side so the JWT verification matches. The publishable key here and the
# secret key there must be from the SAME Clerk application.
#
# Get from: Clerk dashboard → API keys → "Publishable keys".
# VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
